            <ArticleTitle>Rare Popliteal Venous Aneurysm: A Case Report and Review of the Literature.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>491-492</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/1538574417718444</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Popliteal venous aneurysms (PVAs) are rare and may represent a cause of recurrent pulmonary embolism. We present a case of PVA identified on ultrasound for deep venous thrombosis in a 27-year-old female with popliteal fossa pain. We discuss our recommendations for treatment and present a review of the previously reported cases.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
